<title>USA: Clinton pleased negotiators worked in good faith.</title>
<headline>Clinton pleased negotiators worked in good faith.</headline>
<dateline>EDGARTOWN, Mass. 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton thanked representatives of United Parcel Service and the Teamsters union for their &quot;hard work and determination&quot; in reaching a tentative deal to end a 15-day shipping strike.</p>
<p>&quot;I am pleased that the parties negotiated in good faith,&quot; Clinton said in a written statement read to reporters shortly after the settlement was announced.</p>
</text>
